<h2>Dates and place</h2>

<h3>When and where is it?</h3>
<p>{{ summit.dates.display }}, in {{ summit.location.city }}, {{ summit.location.country }}. The specific venue is not confirmed — see <a href="/venue/">Venue</a>.</p>

<h3>Are the dates final?</h3>
<p>Yes. The dates and the city are confirmed by the secretariat and are safe to book flights against.</p>

<h2>Registering</h2>

<h3>What does registering actually do right now?</h3>
<p>It records your interest and the category you fall into, and it puts you on the list that receives fees, venue and programme details before they are published. It is not a ticket and it does not hold a place.</p>

<h3>How much does it cost?</h3>
<p>Fees have not been set. When anyone quotes you a price for this summit, check it came from the secretariat.</p>

<h3>Which category do I choose?</h3>
<p>Delegate to attend the forums and expo; Exhibitor to take a stand; Sponsor for partnership; Government if attending in an official capacity; Media for accreditation; Student at student rate. If two fit, pick the one closest to your reason for coming and say so in the message field.</p>

<h3>Can I change category later?</h3>
<p>Yes. Nothing is binding at this stage.</p>

<h2>The programme</h2>

<h3>Who is speaking?</h3>
<p>No speakers are confirmed yet. The <a href="/speakers/">call for speakers</a> is open.</p>

<h3>Is there a detailed agenda?</h3>
<p>The three day-level themes are confirmed and on the <a href="/programme/">programme</a> page. Session times, rooms and tracks are still being assembled.</p>

<h3>What language will sessions be in?</h3>
<p>Not yet confirmed. Given the audience, interpretation arrangements are something the secretariat is working through.</p>

<h2>Exhibiting and partnership</h2>

<h3>What does a stand cost?</h3>
<p>Not set. Stand sizes, rates and fit-out rules are issued to registered exhibitors first. See <a href="/exhibition/">Exhibition</a>.</p>

<h3>Are any sponsorship tiers taken?</h3>
<p>No. All five are unallocated.</p>

<h2>Practicalities</h2>

<h3>Do I need a visa?</h3>
<p>Kenya operates an electronic travel authorisation for most visitors. Check the official source at <a href="https://www.etakenya.go.ke/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">etakenya.go.ke</a> and your own government's advice. If you need an invitation letter, register and ask.</p>

<h3>Is there a summit hotel?</h3>
<p>The secretariat is arranging accommodation for delegations, but no hotel block or partner is confirmed. Holding off on non-refundable bookings until the venue is announced is the safe move.</p>

<h3>Will sessions be recorded or streamed?</h3>
<p>Not decided.</p>

<h2>About this site</h2>

<h3>Why do so many pages say "to be entered"?</h3>
<p>Because those things are genuinely not decided, and inventing them would mean retracting them later. Anything stated on this site is either confirmed by the secretariat or sourced and dated.</p>

<h3>My question is not here.</h3>
<p><a href="/contact/">Ask the secretariat</a>.</p>
